cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the accompanying article and the collection authors."
type: software
title: "cure2fewshot: a deterministic protocol for converting a pill image collection into a few shot retrieval benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen annotations and expected outputs for a deterministic protocol that converts a public
  pill image collection into a few shot retrieval benchmark aligned with the published low shot
  evaluation protocol of ePillID, together with a scored rubric that decides whether the converted
  result is fit for use. Contains no image: the collection must be obtained from its original
  authors and is not redistributed here.
version: 1.0.2
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hublinhdn/cure2fewshot"
keywords:
  - benchmark construction
  - image retrieval
  - few shot recognition
  - pill identification
  - reproducibility
